.\n\\]\n\nFor any \\((a,b)\\in T_n\\) we have \\(1\\le b\\le n\\), so \\((a,b)\\) lies on \\(L_b\\).  \nAll lines are of the form (3) with slope \\(0\\); therefore they are non‑sunny and \\(k=0\\).\n\n#### 2.2  Exactly one sunny line (\\(k=1\\))\n\nConsider the \\(n-1\\) diagonal lines  \n\n\\[\nD_c:\\;x+y=c\\qquad(c=3,4,\\dots ,n+1)\n\\]\n\n(which are non‑sunny) and add the sunny line  \n\n\\[\nS:\\;y=2x-1 .\n\\]\n\nThe diagonal \\(D_c\\) covers every point of \\(T_n\\) whose sum equals \\(c\\ge3\\).  \nThe only point of \\(T_n\\) not lying on any \\(D_c\\) is \\((1,1)\\) (its sum is \\(2\\)), and \\((1,1)\\) belongs to \\(S\\).  \nThus all points of \\(T_n\\) are covered, and exactly one line (namely \\(S\\)) is sunny.\n\nBoth constructions use \\(n\\) distinct lines, so the values \\(k=0\\) and \\(k=1\\) are indeed attainable for every \\(n\\ge3\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Final classification\n\nFrom (10) we have \\(k\\le1\\); from the constructions of §2 we have \\(k=0\\) and \\(k=1\\) both realizable.  \nHence for every integer \\(n\\ge3\\)\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;k\\in\\{0,1\\}\\;}\n\\]\n\nis the complete set of admissible numbers of sunny lines.\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
